    "short_task": "# Anonymous scalar optimization\n\nOptimize an unknown scalar objective over 12 bounded numerical parameters. Evaluations are deterministic for this fixed task.\n\nObjective: minimize `value`.\n\nBudget: 16 shared initial observations and 48 new evaluations (64 total).\n\n## Submission\n\nProvide one complete finite configuration within the declared parameter types and bounds. Only the host returns objective observations.\n\n## Prior information\n\nUpstream evidence indicates that exactly four parameters affect the objective:\n`x1`, `x4`, `x7`, `x10`. The other eight parameters are inactive and can be held fixed\nwhile optimizing the active subspace.\n\nWithin the active subspace, the objective is smooth and nonseparable. Its\ninteractions are sparse, and low-loss configurations are concentrated around a\nrelatively narrow, curved region. The effect of changing one active parameter may\ntherefore depend on the current values of other active parameters. The main\nlow-loss region is connected.\n\n## Read details as needed\n\nThere are 12 optimizable coordinates. get_search_space supports names, query, optional annotated groups and paged index/details views.\n\nget_task_context sections: overview, submission, prior_information. Read scoring rules and relevant mechanisms before choosing a candidate.\n\nget_trial_history and get_incumbent return scores first; request parameter_names to inspect selected values.\n\nFollow instructions.md: submit_candidate accepts a full config or workspace JSON file directly; write_candidate is optional.\n",
